        <item>
            <title>1.11.0</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 03 Jul 2026 18:20:00 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.11.0</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.11.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[
                <h3>New</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>User Dictionary.</strong> Teach Vox your names, jargon, and spoken shortcuts. The new Dictionary tab in Settings lets you add words and replacements with a live preview — say “my work email” and the address lands in your text; technical terms come out spelled and capitalized right, on every accuracy setting. Sounds-alike matching fixes common mishearings automatically, and your dictionary imports/exports as CSV or JSON.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Fixed</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>No more repeated update prompts.</strong> If Vox kept offering you the same update after installing it, this release cures it for good.</li>
                    <li>Internal test-reliability fixes that make every future release better-verified.</li>
                </ul>
            ]]></description>
